# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Cache policy note: ehd.emit writes stable filenames (index.json, logs.bin,
# values/{site}.json) and overwrites them in place -- there is no content hash
# or version in any path.  A long max-age or `immutable` would therefore pin
# stale ring-width data in visitors' browsers across a pipeline rerun, which
# Cloudflare's edge purge does not fix.  `no-cache` stores the response but
# forces revalidation; Pages emits ETags, so the common case is a 304 with an
# empty body, not a refetch.
#
# If the extra round-trip ever matters, the fix is to version the payload path
# (data/v1/...) in emit.py + app.js, and only then switch to immutable.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/data/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/style.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# ehd.emit writes logs.bin and index.json brotli-compressed at quality 11 --
# Cloudflare's content-type allowlist excludes application/octet-stream, so
# logs.bin shipped raw (84% of first load), and where the edge does compress it
# is tuned for speed: it returns index.json at 345,660 B where `brotli -q 11`
# gets 254,711 B.  Declaring the encoding here is what makes those bytes
# legible to the browser, so these two rules and the compression in emit.py
# have to be changed together -- dropping either one serves brotli as raw
# geometry and the viewer draws nothing.
#
# This does not cost content negotiation, which was the expected objection.
# Measured live 2026-08-20: a client sending `Accept-Encoding: gzip` gets
# index.json re-encoded as gzip (336,872 B) and logs.bin decompressed to its
# raw 1,836,696 B, and a client sending no `Accept-Encoding` gets both raw.
# Cloudflare decodes and re-encodes at the edge, so pre-compressing only
# changes what a br-capable client receives.
#
# app.js checks logs.bin's byte length against n_logs and fails loudly if this
# rule ever stops being applied.

/data/logs.bin
  Content-Encoding: br

/data/index.json
  Content-Encoding: br
